{
  "$comment": [
    "SHARED CONTRACT -- the WALK AGGREGATE seam (S-146, 판정 331).",
    "",
    "THE QUESTION THIS SEAM ASKS: 'what is this group's number?' -- and it is answered TWICE,",
    "once on the server and once in the browser, about the same nodes.",
    "",
    "  Python : `ledger_api.ledger_subgraph.group_nodes(nodes, group_by, measure)`",
    "  JS     : `AGGREGATE[measure]` in `client2/src/rnd_board/api.js`",
    "",
    "WHY THE SEAM EXISTS AT ALL. The client has folded these seven since the board was built,",
    "and it REFUSES to fold a truncated walk (`trendFromWalk`, api.js): at 10^8 the budget cuts",
    "first, so the screen goes blank rather than wrong. S-146 moves the fold to where the",
    "population is whole. That means the same seven names now have two implementations, and the",
    "one that drifts is the one nobody scored.",
    "",
    "WHAT WOULD DIVERGE WITHOUT THIS FILE -- each of these passes both sides' own tests:",
    "  * `mean` of an empty group: 0, null, or NaN. JS `reduce(...)/0` is NaN; the server says",
    "    null, because 0 would claim the values were there and summed to nothing.",
    "  * `median` of an even count: the lower middle, or the mean of the two middles.",
    "  * `distinct` over objects: identity, JSON text, or a canonical form.",
    "  * a PLURAL attribute (S-144): one value picked, or membership in every group it names.",
    "    The server puts the node in BOTH groups -- picking one would decide which of two",
    "    declared-true values counts.",
    "",
    "EXPECTATIONS ARE THE SERVER'S ANSWER, and that is a choice rather than a default: the",
    "server is the side that can see the whole population, so where the two differ it is the",
    "client that moves. C-90 is where that lands."
  ],
  "$shape": {
    "nodes": "the walk's `nodes`, as the response carries them",
    "group_by": "`type`, or the name of a value a node carries",
    "measure": "one of the seven, `name:<attribute>` for the arithmetic five",
    "groups": "[{key, n, value}] sorted by key"
  },
